# Positions that PROBE. The bench list does not: every one of its FENs has more
# men than any table anyone installs for a test run, so the whole tablebase
# reader -- TBFile::map, decompress_pairs, probe_wdl, probe_dtz -- is absent
# from every instruction and counter figure this tree records. A bound placed
# inside decompress_pairs is therefore free according to every perf gate here,
# which is not the same as being free.
#
# Four men, because tests/syzygy holds the 3-4-5 set's 3-man and 4-man tables
# and nothing larger. THIS IS A LOWER BOUND ON THE BLOCK WALK. Block count
# scales with table size, so the two walk loops in decompress_pairs iterate less
# here than they would on a 6-man table, and a cost measured on this list must
# be read as "at least this much", never as "this much".
#
# Blank lines and lines beginning with '#' are not FENs; setup_bench pushes
# every non-empty line, so this file is fed through a filter rather than read
# directly. tests/perfbudget.sh --syzygy does that and prepends the SyzygyPath
# setoption line, which has to name a directory only the caller knows.
#
# Each position is the side to move having to convert or hold: the root ranking
# probes every legal move, and the search probes again at every node inside the
# cardinality. A position already won or lost by mate distance would return
# from the root and probe nothing.
8/8/8/4k3/8/8/3Q4/4K2r w - - 0 1
8/8/8/8/1k1p4/8/1K6/3R4 w - - 0 1
8/8/4k3/8/8/8/4b3/R3K3 w - - 0 1
